{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8edc497cc8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-388","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Umber Tunnel is in central Canada. It opened in 2015.</li><li>Its length is 21 kilometers.</li><li>The Ironwood Tunnel is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 1894.</li><li>Its length is 17 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the Umber Tunnel and the Ironwood Tunnel.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Umber Tunnel opened in 2015, while the Ironwood Tunnel opened in 1894.","Both the Umber Tunnel and the Ironwood Tunnel are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The length of the Umber Tunnel (21 kilometers) is greater than that of the Ironwood Tunnel (17 kilometers).","The Umber Tunnel is in central Canada, and the Ironwood Tunnel is in southern New Zealand."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d64dae8bf5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-395","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Juniper National Park is in southern Norway. It was established in 1995.</li><li>Its area is 2,697 square kilometers.</li><li>Halden National Park is in southern New Zealand. It was established in 1951.</li><li>Its area is 1,211 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between Juniper National Park and Halden National Park.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Juniper National Park is in southern Norway, and Halden National Park is in southern New Zealand.","Both Juniper National Park and Halden National Park are parks known for their old-growth forests.","The area of Juniper National Park (2,697 square kilometers) is greater than that of Halden National Park (1,211 square kilometers).","Juniper National Park was established in 1995, while Halden National Park was established in 1951."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.f697b27716","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-4","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Kowalski is a marine biologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Kowalski recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Kowalski found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","Kowalski found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Marine biologist Nadia Kowalski set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.","To investigate the question, Kowalski recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.09a3312603","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-15","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Oyelaran is a psychologist.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Oyelaran had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Oyelaran found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Psychologist Jonas Oyelaran set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Oyelaran found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Oyelaran concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.7cdbe7e18d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-22","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Takeda is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","To investigate the question, Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Agricultural scientist Priya Takeda set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.259643c88d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-24","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Nakamura is a materials scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Nakamura coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Nakamura found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Materials scientist Ingrid Nakamura set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","Nakamura found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","To investigate the question, Nakamura coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Nakamura concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.9a2664c05f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-38","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Solberg is a sociologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Solberg surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Solberg concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Solberg found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Sociologist Sofia Solberg set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b332559ba6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-39","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Kowalski is a sociologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Sociologist Kofi Kowalski set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a671d4179e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-43","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Halvorsen is a geologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Halvorsen measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Halvorsen found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Halvorsen concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Halvorsen found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","Geologist Amara Halvorsen set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8eff3ea0fb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-47","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Mensah is a geologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Geologist Dmitri Mensah set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.bf17a866e0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-57","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Kowalski is a zoologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","Zoologist Leila Kowalski set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.","Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0119d0a0c3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-67","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Petrov is a linguist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Petrov gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Petrov found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Petrov concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Petrov concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Petrov found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","To investigate the question, Petrov gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Linguist Yara Petrov set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.210860a77b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-83","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Nakamura is a botanist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Nakamura grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Nakamura found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Nakamura grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Botanist Zara Nakamura set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.","Nakamura found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Nakamura concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.67f71292ec","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-84","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Rahman is an urban planner.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Rahman measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Rahman found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Rahman concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Rahman concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","To investigate the question, Rahman measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Rahman found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Urban planner Kofi Rahman set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.f9df0a894c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-86","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Oyelaran is an urban planner.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Urban planner Idris Oyelaran set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.7effb1d3bb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-87","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Mensah is an urban planner.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Urban planner Kwame Mensah set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.736c5a7ef5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-93","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Sato is a hydrologist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Hydrologist Elias Sato set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.481b31ba34","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-98","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Mensah is an education researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Elias Mensah set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a98585d6ed","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-110","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is a primatologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Primatologist Priya Mensah set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","To investigate the question, Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.06415df50c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-113","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Delacroix is a primatologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Delacroix observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Delacroix found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Primatologist Ravi Delacroix set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","To investigate the question, Delacroix observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Delacroix found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.12634f21f7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-114","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Mensah is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Mensah asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Mensah found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Mensah concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mensah asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Sleep researcher Beatriz Mensah set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","Mensah found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Mensah concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b2d55409fc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-115","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Novak is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Sleep researcher Ravi Novak set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","To investigate the question, Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.35c7fb6513","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-133","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Takeda is an archaeologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Takeda analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Takeda found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Takeda concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Takeda found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","Takeda concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Archaeologist Viktor Takeda set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.f22c6c2d92","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-136","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Mbeki is an archaeologist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Mbeki analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Mbeki found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mbeki concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","To investigate the question, Mbeki analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Mbeki found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","Archaeologist Diego Mbeki set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.7ed98ae4b3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-158","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Nakamura is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Nakamura moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Nakamura found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Behavioral economist Yara Nakamura set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.","Nakamura found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","To investigate the question, Nakamura moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d9fec2b3a9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-162","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Abara is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Abara played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Abara found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Abara concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","To investigate the question, Abara played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Abara found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","Veterinary scientist Kenji Abara set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.bdd72b61c4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-170","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Adeyemi is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Forest ecologist Ravi Adeyemi set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients.","Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."}
